\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The EnerHabitat ecosystem. The \texttt  {enerhabitat} Python package is the computational core, organized around the \texttt  {Location}, \texttt  {System}/\texttt  {System2D}, and \texttt  {Config} classes; the Shiny for Python web application provides a graphical interface to the one-dimensional model; and the validation repository verifies the solvers against EnergyPlus and against published guarded hot-plate measurements.}}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{5}{The EnerHabitat ecosystem. The \texttt {enerhabitat} Python package is the computational core, organized around the \texttt {Location}, \texttt {System}/\texttt {System2D}, and \texttt {Config} classes; the Shiny for Python web application provides a graphical interface to the one-dimensional model; and the validation repository verifies the solvers against EnergyPlus and against published guarded hot-plate measurements}{figure.1}{}}
